    assistant: "Ang heterogeneous mixture po ay isang uri ng mixture kung saan ang composition ay HINDI pare-pareho sa buong mixture. Ibig sabihin, nakikita mo ang different parts o components ng mixture.\n\nKatangian ng heterogeneous mixture:\n- Non-uniform composition\n- Makikita mo ang different parts\n- May visible boundaries between components\n- Ang properties ay nagbabago depende sa parteng tinitignan mo\n\nMga halimbawa ng heterogeneous mixture:\n- Halo-halo — nakikita mo ang beans, jelly, leche flan, ice, at milk\n- Trail mix — may nuts, raisins, at chocolate chips\n- Sand and gravel — may maliliit at malalaking particles\n- Pizza — may cheese, pepperoni, vegetables, at crust\n- Salad — may lettuce, tomatoes, cucumber, at dressing\n- Concrete — may cement, sand, gravel, at water\n\nSa Pilipinas, marami tayong heterogeneous mixtures sa pagkain:\n- Arroz caldo — may kanin, manok, garlic, at broth\n- Pancit — may noodles, vegetables, meat, at sauce\n- Bicol express — may karne, gata, sili, at bawang\n- Fruit salad — may various fruits at cream\n\nAng heterogeneous mixture ay madaling i-separate gamit ang physical methods:\n- Hand picking (pag-pick ng components)\n- Filtration (pag-separate ng solid mula liquid)\n- Decantation (pag-buhos ng liquid para ihiwalay sa solid)\n- Magnetism (kung may magnetic components)\n\nAng interesting sa heterogeneous mixtures, minsan kailangan mong i-mix o i-stir bago gamitin para mag-distribute ang components. Halimbawa, ang orange juice na may pulp ay kailangang i-shake bago inumin.\n\nSa iyong bahay, ano ang mga heterogeneous mixtures na nakikita mo sa kusina?"
